# A VHS script that records the 90-second demo to a GIF, deterministically.
#
#   brew install vhs        # or: go install github.com/charmbracelet/vhs@latest
#   cd <repo root>
#   vhs examples/temporal_memory_demo/demo.tape
#
# Output lands at examples/temporal_memory_demo/demo.gif. VHS drives a headless
# terminal, so the result does not depend on the recording machine's font, theme, or
# how steadily anybody types — re-running it produces the same GIF.
#
# The GIF is NOT checked in. It is roughly 2-4 MB, it is a build product of this file
# and demo.py, and a binary that has to be regenerated by hand every time the script
# changes is a binary that goes stale. Generate it when you need one.

Output examples/temporal_memory_demo/demo.gif

Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 16
Set Width 1000
Set Height 760
Set Padding 24
Set Theme "Catppuccin Mocha"
# The demo paces itself, so VHS records in real time rather than typing anything.
Set TypingSpeed 40ms
Set PlaybackSpeed 1.0

Type "python3 examples/temporal_memory_demo/demo.py"
Enter
# demo.py runs for about 90 seconds. Sleep past the end of it, then hold the closing
# frame so the last screen is readable in a loop.
Sleep 95s
Sleep 4s
